What matters is how much useful experience they can learn from.

@axisrobotics is building this layer through simulation and human interaction, turning

content:
No matter how advanced a robot's model gets, it still struggles without solid real-world data to learn from.  https://t.co/nmStQr0Abg

@axisrobotics  is taking a genuinely interesting approach here: turning simple browser-based interactions into actual training data for Physical AI. No need to buy a robot, no complicated wallet setup, you literally just log in and start contributing.

And the numbers back it up. They've already crossed 150,000 contributors, 3.7 million trajectories, and over 42,000 hours of data collected. This isn't some pitch deck concept anymore, it's already live and running. 🤖

